And we also have the server authenticate himself to a client.

00:08:30.769 --> 00:08:35.489
So there's two-way authentication. Because sometimes when Amazon has to

00:08:35.489 --> 00:08:38.008
authenticate himself to be Amazon, right?

00:08:38.328 --> 00:08:42.129
So that's a server reports an identity to a client.

00:08:42.448 --> 00:08:46.109
So we have two-way authentication happening in reality.

00:08:46.489 --> 00:08:51.159
And the steps very easy. So, um, normally we

00:08:51.159 --> 00:08:55.080
initiate and then the challenge, OK, who you are,

