and then proof, right, send this proof. And then

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:18.419
the server will validate in his end, will check the proof

00:09:18.419 --> 00:09:23.179
and then pass or fail, right? So this is the obvious steps.

00:09:23.599 --> 00:09:26.599
And now we talk about the zones in authentication.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.599
There's a zone 1, client zone, transmission zone,

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:34.390
zone 2, and the server zone, zone 3. Right,

00:09:35.179 --> 00:09:39.820
when we design a good authentication protocol with which all these three

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:44.229
zones are considered, are covered very well,

